 ("3.3 DERECOGNITION", "3.3.2", "Extinguishment and substantial modification", "A financial liability (and by analogy an asset whose terms are substantially modified) is derecognised when the terms are substantially different; a modification that is not substantial is accounted for under 5.4.3.", PART,
  "Built 14 October 2026 (uncommitted): the 10 percent test of B3.3.6 by analogy against the governed modification_threshold, with the qualitative factors (counterparty, currency, SPPI, instrument) recorded on the register; at or above it, or with a factor, the loan is derecognised and version N+1 recognised at its recorded fair value with a new EIR; a credit-impaired loan derecognised this way is POCI and fails closed (no credit-adjusted EIR is held). Nothing is confirmed on the scratch clone.", "Until 14 October 2026 this row was Outstanding.", "Partially done: built; review item R14 records that the 10 percent test is written for liabilities, so it is MAIIC's governed asset policy.", CALC, "modification_threshold", "Tests\\Feature\\Eir\\ModificationAccountingTest::test_a_change_at_or_above_the_threshold_derecognises_and_fails_closed_without_a_fair_value; Tests\\Feature\\Eir\\ModificationAccountingTest::test_a_qualitative_factor_derecognises_whatever_the_ten_percent_test_says; Tests\\Feature\\Eir\\ModificationAccountingTest::test_a_credit_impaired_loan_derecognised_is_poci_and_fails_closed"),
